he scored goals at every major Club he  played for but it was at Aston Villa  where de lien Atkinson really made his  name in the 1990s the 48 year old had  been tasered by police in this  cul-de-sac near his father's home in  Telford an investigation by the  independent office for police conduct  found there had also been a period of  restraint and other uses of force mr.  Atkinson went into cardiac arrest in an  ambulance on the way to hospital and  died one police constable has been  charged with the murder of daylian  Atkinson a second officer has been  charged with assault causing actual  bodily harm we're not able to name  either officer because it was argued in  court that identification would infringe  their right to life both officers have  been released on bail  relatives of mr. Atkinson said he'd been  suffering from a weak heart  in a statement their lawyer said Dale  Ian's family welcomes the decision to  put the conduct of police officers  before a jury but regrets that already  more than three years have passed since  daylian died the court heard about mr.  Atkinson's career at Aston Villa the  prosecution said it must consider  whether Birmingham was the appropriate  venue for a trial given what they called  the strong feelings about his death in  some parts of the community  Lisa down Sky News Birmingham
 

